17
00:01:44.284 --> 00:01:53.862
Grammar time! Present continuous for now. Listen. It is raining now. The wind is blowing hard.

18
00:01:53.912 --> 00:01:59.700
Your turn. Say it with me. It is raining now. The wind is blowing hard.

19
00:02:04.677 --> 00:02:11.330
The forecast says a thunderstorm is coming, with heavy downpour later. It has been sweltering and humid all week.

20
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.698
I like this story!

21
00:02:14.005 --> 00:02:19.180
Look! What's the word?

22
00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.450
Thunderstorm!

23
00:02:21.482 --> 00:02:26.702
Look! What's the word?

24
00:02:26.752 --> 00:02:27.876
Chilly!

25
00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:37.083
Think and answer. What is the weather usually like in your favorite season?

26
00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:38.283
Great answer!

27
00:02:39.457 --> 00:02:43.789
Great work today! See you next time. Bye-bye!

28
